# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check the status {#check-the-status}"
msgstr "Vérifier le statut {#check-the-status}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Immediately after you call `run()`, the status is usually `QUEUED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Juste après avoir appelé `run()`, le statut est généralement `QUEUED` :\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Status | Meaning |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `QUEUED` | The job waits for a compute slot. |\n"
"| `INITIALIZING` | The workflow is starting an environment with the job's compute profile. |\n"
"| `RUNNING` | The workflow's entrypoint is running. |\n"
"| `RUNNING: <stage>` | The entrypoint reported a stage with [`update_status()`](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status), such as `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU`. |\n"
"| `CANCELING` | You canceled the job, and the workflow is stopping it. |\n"
"| `DONE` | The entrypoint exited successfully. |\n"
"| `ERROR` | The entrypoint raised an error or exited with a nonzero code. See [Find the cause of an error](#find-the-cause-of-an-error). |\n"
"| `CANCELED` | You canceled the job, or it reached the [24-hour limit](#time-limit). |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Statut | Signification |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `QUEUED` | Le job attend un emplacement de calcul. |\n"
"| `INITIALIZING` | Le workflow démarre un environnement avec le profil de calcul du job. |\n"
"| `RUNNING` | Le point d'entrée du workflow s'exécute. |\n"
"| `RUNNING: <stage>` | Le point d'entrée a signalé une étape avec [`update_status()`](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status), par exemple `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU`. |\n"
"| `CANCELING` | Tu as annulé le job, et le workflow est en train de l'arrêter. |\n"
"| `DONE` | Le point d'entrée s'est terminé avec succès. |\n"
"| `ERROR` | Le point d'entrée a levé une erreur ou s'est terminé avec un code non nul. Consulte [Trouver la cause d'une erreur](#find-the-cause-of-an-error). |\n"
"| `CANCELED` | Tu as annulé le job, ou il a atteint la [limite de 24 heures](#time-limit). |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`DONE`, `ERROR`, and `CANCELED` are final, and `job.in_terminal_state()` returns `True` for them. A status loop that waits for another value, such as `SUCCEEDED`, never ends.\n"
msgstr "`DONE`, `ERROR` et `CANCELED` sont des statuts finaux, et `job.in_terminal_state()` renvoie `True` pour eux. Une boucle de statut qui attend une autre valeur, comme `SUCCEEDED`, ne se termine jamais.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Wait for the job to end {#wait-for-the-job-to-end}"
msgstr "Attendre la fin du job {#wait-for-the-job-to-end}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To wait until the job ends, call `wait_for_final_state()`. It returns the final status, and with `verbose=True` it prints each status change. If you set `timeout` in seconds, `wait_for_final_state()` raises a `TimeoutError` when the time runs out before the job ends. The job keeps running:\n"
msgstr "Pour attendre la fin du job, appelle `wait_for_final_state()`. Elle renvoie le statut final, et avec `verbose=True` elle affiche chaque changement de statut. Si tu définis `timeout` en secondes, `wait_for_final_state()` lève une `TimeoutError` lorsque le délai expire avant la fin du job. Le job continue de s'exécuter :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`wait_for_final_state()` checks the status after 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, and 32 seconds, and then every 60 seconds, so it sees the end of a short job within seconds and makes few requests for a long job. To check at a fixed interval instead, pass `poll_interval` in seconds.\n"
msgstr "`wait_for_final_state()` vérifie le statut après 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 et 32 secondes, puis toutes les 60 secondes, de sorte qu'elle détecte la fin d'un job court en quelques secondes et fait peu de requêtes pour un job long. Pour vérifier plutôt à intervalle fixe, passe `poll_interval` en secondes.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read the logs {#read-the-logs}"
msgstr "Lire les logs {#read-the-logs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anything that the workflow writes to standard output or standard error goes to the job's logs. You can read them with `job.logs()` while the job runs, before it has a result:\n"
msgstr "Tout ce que le workflow écrit sur la sortie standard ou la sortie d'erreur standard va dans les logs du job. Tu peux les lire avec `job.logs()` pendant l'exécution du job, avant qu'il ait un résultat :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow uploads new log lines about every 15 seconds, and one last time when the job ends or is canceled. Immediately after a job starts, `job.logs()` returns `No logs yet.`\n"
msgstr "Le workflow téléverse les nouvelles lignes de log environ toutes les 15 secondes, et une dernière fois quand le job se termine ou est annulé. Juste après le démarrage d'un job, `job.logs()` renvoie `No logs yet.`\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow keeps the newest 50 MB of logs for each job, and adds a line at the top that says the logs were truncated.\n"
msgstr "Le workflow conserve les 50 Mo de logs les plus récents pour chaque job, et ajoute en haut une ligne indiquant que les logs ont été tronqués.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To decide what your workflow logs, see [Write logs](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#write-logs). To show only the lines that match a regular expression, pass `include` to `job.filtered_logs()`. To hide lines, pass `exclude`.\n"
msgstr "Pour décider de ce que ton workflow journalise, consulte [Écrire des logs](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#write-logs). Pour n'afficher que les lignes qui correspondent à une expression régulière, passe `include` à `job.filtered_logs()`. Pour masquer des lignes, passe `exclude`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get the result {#get-the-result}"
msgstr "Obtenir le résultat {#get-the-result}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.result()` waits until the job ends, then returns the value that the workflow passed to [`save_result()`](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results):\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"`job.result()` attend la fin du job, puis renvoie la valeur que le workflow a transmise à [`save_result()`](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results) :\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By default, `job.result()` checks the status every 30 seconds and waits with no time limit. Pass `maxwait` to limit the number of checks. For example, `job.result(maxwait=40)` waits about 20 minutes. To check one time without waiting, pass `wait=False`. If `job.result()` stops waiting before the job ends, it returns `{}`.\n"
msgstr "Par défaut, `job.result()` vérifie le statut toutes les 30 secondes et attend sans limite de temps. Passe `maxwait` pour limiter le nombre de vérifications. Par exemple, `job.result(maxwait=40)` attend environ 20 minutes. Pour vérifier une seule fois sans attendre, passe `wait=False`. Si `job.result()` cesse d'attendre avant la fin du job, il renvoie `{}`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check how long each stage took {#check-how-long-each-stage-took}"
msgstr "Vérifier la durée de chaque étape {#check-how-long-each-stage-took}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.events()` lists every status and stage change of a job with its time, so you can see how long the job waited for compute and how long each stage took:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"`job.events()` liste chaque changement de statut et d'étape d'un job avec son horodatage, ce qui te permet de voir combien de temps le job a attendu le calcul et combien de temps chaque étape a duré :\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The events use the stored status names. `PENDING` is `INITIALIZING`, and `SUCCEEDED` is `DONE`. For the QPU usage of a run, see [Find the QPU jobs of a run](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#find-the-qpu-jobs-of-a-run).\n"
msgstr "Les événements utilisent les noms de statut stockés. `PENDING` correspond à `INITIALIZING`, et `SUCCEEDED` correspond à `DONE`. Pour l'utilisation de QPU d'une exécution, consulte [Trouver les jobs QPU d'une exécution](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#find-the-qpu-jobs-of-a-run).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Find the cause of an error {#find-the-cause-of-an-error}"
msgstr "Trouver la cause d'une erreur {#find-the-cause-of-an-error}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When the workflow raises an exception, the job ends with the `ERROR` status. For example, run the workflow with an angle that it rejects:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Quand le workflow lève une exception, le job se termine avec le statut `ERROR`. Par exemple, exécute le workflow avec un angle qu'il rejette :\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The logs show the traceback:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Les logs affichent la trace d'appels :\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.result()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"`job.result()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the workflow [reports errors with `send_error()`](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error), read them with `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")`, and read their messages with `job.error_message()`. For a job without reported errors, `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` returns an empty list, and `job.error_message()` returns `{}`.\n"
msgstr "Si le workflow [signale les erreurs avec `send_error()`](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error), lis-les avec `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")`, et lis leurs messages avec `job.error_message()`. Pour un job sans erreur signalée, `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` renvoie une liste vide, et `job.error_message()` renvoie `{}`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: for custom workflows on Fleets, a raised ServerlessError is not recorded as an error event: only provider jobs run inside gateway/templates/main.tmpl, which calls send_error(). Custom jobs run the entrypoint directly through fleet_custom_job_wrapper.py. Confirm whether custom jobs should get the same handler, and whether error_message() should return a string instead of {}. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Manage jobs {#manage-jobs}"
msgstr "Gérer les jobs {#manage-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cancel a job {#cancel-a-job}"
msgstr "Annuler un job {#cancel-a-job}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Cancel a job with `job.cancel()`. The status changes to `CANCELING` while the workflow stops the job, and then to `CANCELED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Annule un job avec `job.cancel()`. Le statut passe à `CANCELING` pendant que le workflow arrête le job, puis à `CANCELED` :\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.cancel()` returns a message about the job and about its [linked QPU jobs](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs), which it also tries to cancel. For a running job, the workflow sends `SIGTERM` to your entrypoint. To save partial results, see [Clean up when a job is canceled](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled). If the job already ended, `job.cancel()` returns `Job already in terminal state.` and changes nothing.\n"
msgstr "`job.cancel()` renvoie un message sur le job et sur ses [jobs QPU liés](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs), qu'il tente aussi d'annuler. Pour un job en cours d'exécution, le workflow envoie `SIGTERM` à ton point d'entrée. Pour enregistrer des résultats partiels, consulte [Nettoyer lorsqu'un job est annulé](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled). Si le job est déjà terminé, `job.cancel()` renvoie `Job already in terminal state.` et ne change rien.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: in a live test (1 Nov 2026), a job canceled while RUNNING went to CANCELING and then DONE, with its result saved, because the entrypoint finished before the stop took effect. Confirm whether a job that finishes during CANCELING should end as DONE or CANCELED. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Find a job from a new session {#find-a-job-from-a-new-session}"
msgstr "Retrouver un job depuis une nouvelle session {#find-a-job-from-a-new-session}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `Job` object and the workflow exist only in your current Python session. After you restart a notebook kernel, pass the saved job ID to `client.job()`, or list your recent jobs with `client.jobs()`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"L'objet `Job` et le workflow n'existent que dans ta session Python actuelle. Après le redémarrage d'un noyau de notebook, passe l'ID de job enregistré à `client.job()`, ou liste tes jobs récents avec `client.jobs()` :\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`client.jobs()` returns your 10 most recent jobs, newest first. Filter it with `function`, `status` (from the [status table](#check-the-status)), or `created_after` (an ISO 8601 timestamp), and page through it with `limit` and `offset`. To list the workflows that you uploaded, call `client.list()`.\n"
msgstr "`client.jobs()` renvoie tes 10 jobs les plus récents, du plus récent au plus ancien. Filtre-les avec `function`, `status` (d'après le [tableau des statuts](#check-the-status)) ou `created_after` (un horodatage ISO 8601), et parcours-les avec `limit` et `offset`. Pour lister les workflows que tu as téléversés, appelle `client.list()`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads) table on IBM Quantum Platform also lists your jobs, with their status, compute profile, and run times.\n"
msgstr "Le tableau [Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads) sur IBM Quantum Platform liste aussi tes jobs, avec leur statut, leur profil de calcul et leurs durées d'exécution.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Time limit {#time-limit}"
msgstr "Limite de temps {#time-limit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow cancels a job that runs for more than 24 hours, and the job ends with the `CANCELED` status. During long runs, [save checkpoints to file storage](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs) so that you do not lose work.\n"
msgstr "Un workflow géré annule un job qui s'exécute pendant plus de 24 heures, et le job se termine avec le statut `CANCELED`. Pendant les longues exécutions, [enregistre des points de contrôle dans le stockage de fichiers](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs) pour ne pas perdre ton travail.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: the timeout is measured from the job's latest event, not from its start (gateway/scheduler/tasks/update_fleets_jobs_statuses.py stop_job_if_timeout). Calls to update_status() and send_error() create events, so a job that reports stages can run longer than 24 hours. This looks like a bug; confirm the intended behavior. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshoot jobs {#troubleshoot-jobs}"
msgstr "Dépanner les jobs {#troubleshoot-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Problem | Cause |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `run()` fails with `Code: 429` and `Active job limit reached.` | You reached the [active job limit](/guides/run-parameter-sweep#active-job-limit). Wait for some jobs to end, or [cancel](#cancel-a-job) jobs that you no longer need. |\n"
"| The job stays `QUEUED`, and `run()` warned that `your account, plan or subscription is blocked`. | The job does not start until the block on your account, plan, or subscription is lifted. Contact your administrator. |\n"
"| `job.logs()` returns `No logs yet.` | The job is queued or just started. Wait about 15 seconds. |\n"
"| `job.result()` returns `{}` | The job has not ended, was canceled, or saved no result. See [Save results](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results). |\n"
"| `job.error_message()` returns `{}` | The workflow raised an exception without reporting an error. Read the traceback with `job.logs()`. |\n"
"| The job is `CANCELED`, but you did not cancel it | The job reached the [24-hour limit](#time-limit). |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Problème | Cause |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `run()` échoue avec `Code: 429` et `Active job limit reached.` | Tu as atteint la [limite de jobs actifs](/guides/run-parameter-sweep#active-job-limit). Attends la fin de certains jobs, ou [annule](#cancel-a-job) les jobs dont tu n'as plus besoin. |\n"
"| Le job reste `QUEUED`, et `run()` a averti que `your account, plan or subscription is blocked`. | Le job ne démarre pas tant que le blocage de ton compte, plan ou abonnement n'est pas levé. Contacte ton administrateur. |\n"
"| `job.logs()` renvoie `No logs yet.` | Le job est en file d'attente ou vient de démarrer. Attends environ 15 secondes. |\n"
"| `job.result()` renvoie `{}` | Le job n'est pas terminé, a été annulé ou n'a enregistré aucun résultat. Consulte [Enregistrer les résultats](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results). |\n"
"| `job.error_message()` renvoie `{}` | Le workflow a levé une exception sans signaler d'erreur. Lis la trace d'appels avec `job.logs()`. |\n"
"| Le job est `CANCELED`, mais tu ne l'as pas annulé | Le job a atteint la [limite de 24 heures](#time-limit). |\n"

